.TH FIGMA-FONT-AGENT 1 "2026-11-15" "figma-font-agent 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
figma-font-agent \- serve Linux system fonts to Figma in the browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B figma-font-agent
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B figma-font-agent
is a small loopback HTTP service that implements the local font protocol used
by Figma for the web. It indexes the fonts known to fontconfig (and the fonts
in the user's font directories), then answers the requests Figma sends to
\fBhttp://127.0.0.1:44950/figma/\fR.
.PP
The service listens on loopback only. It never writes to the font
directories, contacts the network, or reports telemetry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read configuration from \fIPATH\fR instead of
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/figma-font-agent/config.json\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-config
Write an example configuration file to the default location and exit. An
existing file is never overwritten.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Listen on \fIPORT\fR. May be repeated to listen on several ports. The default
is 44950 with 44960 as a fallback.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preview
Disable the font preview endpoint.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-index
Print the JSON payload that \fB/figma/font-files\fR would return, then exit.
Useful for debugging what Figma will see.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is a JSON object. Every key is optional.
.TP
.B package
String reported to Figma by the version endpoint (default "126.11.9").
.TP
.B version
Numeric protocol version reported to Figma (default 24).
.TP
.B ports
Array of loopback ports to bind (default [44950, 44960]).
.TP
.B font_directories
Array of extra directories to scan for fonts.
.TP
.B rescan_interval_secs
How often to look for new or changed fonts, in seconds. 0 disables rescans
(default 300).
.TP
.B enable_preview
Boolean; set to false to disable the font preview endpoint (default true).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LISTEN_FDS ", " LISTEN_PID
When started by systemd socket activation, the agent serves the passed
listening sockets instead of binding ports itself. Both variables are consumed
and cleared at startup.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Used to locate the configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/figma-font-agent/config.json
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fonts ", " ~/.fonts
User font directories that are always scanned in addition to fontconfig's
list.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground with request logging:
.PP
.nf
    figma-font-agent -v
.fi
.PP
Force a rescan after installing a font:
.PP
.nf
    curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:44950/figma/clear-data
.fi
.PP
Inspect the font list Figma will receive:
.PP
.nf
    figma-font-agent --print-index | jq '.fontFiles | length'
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The service binds to 127.0.0.1 only, restricts CORS to
\fIhttps://www.figma.com\fR, validates the \fBHost\fR header to defeat
DNS rebinding, and serves only paths that are present in its own font index.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full protocol and reverse-engineering notes:
.UR https://github.com/hominluo/figma-font-installer-for-linux
.UE
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/hominluo/figma-font-installer-for-linux/issues
.UE
